From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a webview's page asks the shell to show its dialogs

A <webview> guest's WebContentsDelegate gives content a
JavaScriptDialogManager that sends `alert()`, `confirm()` and `prompt()`
to the element (components/domicile/browser/web_view_guest.cc). The
element fires `DomicileDialogEvent` for the shell to answer.

This patch carries the parts in files Chromium owns: three lists, so
that `DomicileDialogEvent` is compiled and reaches the page, as patch
0103 does for permission requests.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/generated_in_core.gni | 2 ++
 third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/idl_in_core.gni       | 1 +
 third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/build.gni            | 2 ++
 3 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

